.TH BLUEDRAGON 1 "October 2026" "bluedragon 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bluedragon \- configure the M711 gaming mouse
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bluedragon
[\fB\-d\fR \fIDEVICE\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads and changes the settings stored in the M711 mouse (USB 04d9:fc30) over its
hidraw configuration interface. Profiles are numbered 1 to 5.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B dump
Show the active profile, polling rates, and for each profile the LED, DPI levels and buttons.
.TP
\fBread\fR \fIADDR\fR \fILEN\fR
Hex dump device memory.
.TP
\fBwrite\fR \fIADDR\fR \fIBYTE\fR...
Raw write of hex bytes, without applying.
.TP
\fBcommit\fR \fIFLAG\fR
Send an apply command (1 profile, 2 DPI, 4 buttons, 8 polling).
.TP
\fBprofile\fR \fIN\fR
Select the active profile.
.TP
\fBdpi\fR \fIPROFILE\fR \fILEVEL\fR \fIDPI\fR
Set a DPI level (1\-5) to a multiple of 100 between 100 and 5000.
.TP
\fBpolling\fR \fIPROFILE\fR \fIHZ\fR
Set the polling rate: 125, 250, 500 or 1000.
.TP
\fBbutton\fR \fIPROFILE\fR \fIBUTTON\fR \fIACTION\fR
Assign an action to a button slot (0\-11), for example \fBleft\fR, \fBdpi+\fR, \fBvolup\fR,
\fBkey:ctrl+c\fR or \fBraw:8d000000\fR.
.TP
\fBled\fR \fIPROFILE\fR \fBcolor\fR \fIRRGGBB\fR | \fBmode\fR \fIN\fR | \fBvalue\fR \fIN\fR | \fBlevel\fR \fIN\fR
Change the LED settings of a profile.
.TP
\fBmeasure\fR [\fISECONDS\fR]
Measure the real report rate; keep moving the mouse.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-bluedragon.rules
Gives the logged-in user access to the mouse.
.SH AUTHOR
Giovani Avelar.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bluedragon\-gui (1)
